Divex works magic and carries bombs, and travels with [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]], [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]] and [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] as [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]]. He can hide the company from sight, and keeps what he carries in his shadow: the [[Phenomena/Althane/Godpiercer|godpiercer]], and a great store of small wind-up watches. When the others find something enchanted, he is the one who says what it is.

He was born in the blood lake at the heart of [[Geography/Althane/Lunae Badlands/Hidden Gulch/New Haven|New Haven]] and swam in it as a child. He was framed, long before the Weft's work, for stealing a set of costly artifacts; the thief was [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech]], who handed the goods to [[People/Althane/Rowan|Rowan]] and never collected them. Divex did not know who had taken them until he learned that the Broker was Tech.

He carries the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] in his skull and neck.

After [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the Deep]] was destroyed, Divex took the succession of the [[Org/Althane/The Trust|Trust]] in hand and set [[People/Althane/Oxus|Oxus]] over it, then took the [[People/Althane/The Broker|Broker]]'s empty place in the [[Org/Althane/The Network|Network]], where no client had ever known the name behind the messages. He is the foremost living student of [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]] on Althane. He gathered the magic centers of the world into one body, X-Dive, and began a floating city of that name above [[Geography/Althane/Illyara/index|Illyara]], to be run on an engine fed by the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] Beast at New Haven.
